    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and it passes. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and dropped the per-city sequence number entirely.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced `nextCustomerCode` (which built `CITY3-LAST3-NNNN` from a per-city counter) with `customerCodeFor`:\n- **REGION** = the owner's canonical region (`Owner.getRegion()`, which is postcode-derived with a city fallback), rendered `UNKNOWN` when no known region so the token stays a valid `[A-Z0-9]+`.\n- **HASH8** = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`, reusing the existing `shaHex(...)` helper. The telephone is already normalized to E.164 on the owner by the time the code is built.\n- No `findAllOwners()` scan / sequence anymore.\n\nEverything downstream moved to the new identity automatically because it reads `customerCode`:\n- **membershipNumber** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and **checkDigit** (Luhn over the digits in `customerCode`) in `OwnerMapper` now derive from the region-and-hash code.\n- The **create audit record** logs the new `customerCode`.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `localityRegion(owner)` previously called `owner.getRegion()` directly; it now parses the REGION segment out of the `customerCode` (the part before the first `-`), treating the `UNKNOWN` sentinel and a missing code as `null`, which `locality(...)` still renders as `UNKNOWN`. This keeps locality identical in value while sourcing it from the new identity.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` (asserting `customerCode` matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`) passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
